// a `T?` never narrows back on its own. that one-way rule is the whole safety story: widening discards a
// guarantee, which is always safe, while narrowing *asserts* one and needs somewhere to put the failure -
// which is exactly what `guard`, `??` and `?->` are

class Node { int32 $tag; }

Node? $some = Node(1);

Node $narrowed = $some;
